### Example 
I created a simple app w/ the following config props:
```java
@ConfigurationProperties(prefix = "foo")
public class TestConfigProps {

    /**
     * Paths of things
     */
    private List<File> paths = new ArrayList<>(Collections.singletonList(new File(".")));

    public List<File> getPaths() {
        return paths;
    }

    public void setPaths(final List<File> paths) {
        this.paths = paths;
    }
}
```

#### Warn Mode
- I ran the config processor which output the following:

  <img width="1432" alt="Screen Shot 2021-09-18 at 10 42 33 AM" src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/28907971/133894673-39847a9f-a739-47d9-b0ef-a187aae58f8d.png">
  
- I then added the following hint:
  ```json
  {
    "properties": [
      {
        "name": "foo.paths",
        "type": "java.util.List<java.io.File>",
        "defaultValue": [
          "."
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
  ```
- I ran the config processor again - problem fixed:

  <img width="1180" alt="Screen Shot 2021-09-18 at 10 43 19 AM" src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/28907971/133894708-a3353605-c6e8-4aef-bc07-2701ea381a75.png">

#### Fail Mode

When using "fail mode" its the same as above w/ the exception of the problem output looking like the following:

  <img width="1433" alt="Screen Shot 2021-09-18 at 10 44 21 AM" src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/28907971/133894807-612594dd-2804-40f6-8dc9-4d996a89c1e3.png">




### TODOS
- [ ]  add ability to disable error mode??
- [ ]  add test for configprocessor validation checks
- [ ]  docs?

Fixes gh-28039

